Package: voiageR
Type: Package
Title: Value of Information Analysis in R
Version: 1.0.0
Author: voiage Development Team
Maintainer: voiage Development Team <voiage@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: An R interface to the Rust-backed voiage core for Value of Information analysis,
    with direct Rust C ABI paths for EVPI and canonical contract validation, optional Arrow
    interchange, and helper functions for Python environment management where advanced
    compatibility methods still use reticulate. Provides functions for calculating Expected Value of Perfect Information
    (EVPI), Expected Value of Partial Perfect Information (EVPPI), and Expected Value of
    Sample Information (EVSI).
URL: https://github.com/edithatogo/voiage
BugReports: https://github.com/edithatogo/voiage/issues
License: Apache License (>= 2.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: no
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: voiage Rust C ABI library; Python (>= 3.12) only for compatibility methods
Imports:
    jsonlite (>= 1.8)
Suggests:
    arrow (>= 16.0.0),
    reticulate (>= 1.20),
    knitr (>= 1.45),
    rmarkdown (>= 2.26),
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
